        "content": "\nNone of these are runnable yet (the pieces they exercise are stubs), but scaffold them now so implementation is TDD'd against a real target rather than \"seems to work\":\n\n1. **Full run lifecycle** (`POST /runs` → background `execute_run` → `entities`/`matches`/`conflicts`/`resolutions` rows → `GET /runs/:id/status` reaches `\"complete\"`). Needs a test Postgres (or `testcontainers-python`) since `db.py` writes directly.\n2. **Table-ownership guard** — an integration test that runs the full pipeline against a scratch DB and asserts the engine issued zero writes to `sources` or `rulesets`, and the web layer (once route handlers exist) issues zero writes to `entities`/`matches`/`conflicts`. This is the single most important invariant in AGENTS.md and currently has no enforcement, automated or otherwise.\n3. **Web API route handlers** — `web/app/api/` is empty; none of the routes in AGENTS.md's route table exist yet. Flagging as not-yet-buildable, but note it so it isn't missed once `runs/route.ts`, `conflicts/[id]/resolution/route.ts` etc. land — each needs a Zod-validation-rejects test per AGENTS.md's \"every route handler validates its body with Zod, no exceptions.\"\n4. **eval harness end-to-end** — `generate` → all three systems via `run_system` → `write_results_table`/`plot_threshold_sweep` producing real files in `docs/results/`. A `--quick` smoke variant belongs in CI once Phase 2/6 land.\n5. **Rulesets versioning invariant** — once `POST /rulesets` exists: assert it always creates a new row/version and never mutates an existing one (AGENTS.md: \"Rulesets are versioned, never edited in place\").\n\n```python\n",
